  "id": "speaking/after-a-cut-the-classifier-policy-resumes-when-the-turn-leaves-the-agent-free-to-go-on",
  "title": "After its answer was cut, the classifier policy also judges whether the turn leaves the agent free to go on: free, and neither asked for quiet nor talking over an unfinished speaker, the agent speaks with the reason resume after cut, its notes asking it to go on from where it was cut; otherwise the turn decides as without the cut",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4",
    "§6.8",
    "§12.3.13"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-6.4-213",
    "RK-6.4-214"
  ],
  "notes": "In each room the agent answers Alice, a voice channel of the room records that answer cut 1.2 s in, and Alice speaks again. The classifier then reads what the agent was saying and how long it was heard, and is asked whether the turn leaves it free to go on. In r1 it is, and the agent resumes, the note of its turn saying to go on from where it was cut without repeating what was heard (the note's wording is the implementation's; the scenario matches the clause the RFC gives it); in r2 the turn wants the floor; in r3 Alice asks for quiet; in r4 she has not finished. Python: speaking/classifier.py RESUME, resume_after_cut.",
  "requires_features": [
    "voice"
  ],
